4739111001-baba6baa-84e2-4a0a-b170-c7644ae17888"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787095131772288001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0fa31637-4b25-45d6-935c-9b1438b007c7","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"6633-219e-988a-42f6"},{"link_uuid":"a56ff398-0fd7-4fae-bb55-2ec1827335f3","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"d074-ab22-e37a-4480"},{"link_uuid":"c63a34dd-3b9f-4af9-ab18-9ece254f22d8","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"9515-ffa1-5272-4310"},{"link_uuid":"70b44a48-4510-49cf-93a3-ffef7b73821e","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"1b07-bf4d-4aca-41c4"},{"link_uuid":"eb0f6457-e667-4f79-8ebe-18093ca77836","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"9e42-78f7-c164-4bc8"},{"link_uuid":"9a0bf7a5-1fec-40c9-9013-9189ecd1444f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"80a7-7832-83d2-44e8"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nSlice C1 (ticket 29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8) recorded 11 below-seam ambient config/credential reads across the residual scattered readers (_logging, _opcert_signing, _operation_config, mirror_guard, review_bot/app, signing — 7 rows) AND the grounding subsystem (grounding/harness, grounding/oracle, grounding/resolve — 4 rows) as entries in `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS`. These grounding rows belong to no earlier slice, so this residual slice folds them in alongside the other scattered readers. RP-04 is not complete while these ambient reads sit below the approved composition/credential/backend seams enforced by `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`. Parent: 075b-1479-dcb7-40ab.\n\nAffected files (relative to `src/rebar/`):\n  - `src/rebar/_logging.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_operation_config.py`\n  - `src/rebar/mirror_guard.py`\n  - `src/rebar/review_bot/app.py`\n  - `src/rebar/signing.py`\n  - `src/rebar/grounding/harness.py` (L56: dynamic `os.environ.get`)\n  - `src/rebar/grounding/oracle.py` (L170: `load_config()` below seam)\n  - `src/rebar/grounding/resolve.py` (L62 import-time `REBAR_CTAGS_BIN` default capture; L543 `load_config()` below seam)\n\nThis slice drains the 11 residual/grounding rows (9 files). It does NOT assert whole-tree EMPTY: two `binding_lifecycle.py` rows (`RECONCILER_ABSENT_RETIRE_GRACE` + its `_env_int`/`os.environ.get` parser) are OUTSIDE this slice's scope — they were MOVED into `binding_lifecycle.py` by RP-02 S2 and their cut-to-seam is the RP-04 S7.3.a retarget tracked by ticket `01d8-c18d-b229-419a` (best-kingly-monkey). The whole-tree list reaches EMPTY only once BOTH this slice and that retarget land; whichever lands last observes EMPTY.\n\n## Outcome\nEvery below-seam read in the files above is either (a) CUT to compose through the approved seam that already assembles config — the operation snapshot (`rebar._operation_config.OperationSnapshot` / `compose_operation_snapshot`), a startup binding, or the provider-credential boundary — or (b) for a genuine subsystem kill-switch / test-only control that has no place in the operation snapshot, annotated in place with an inline `# read-via: <reason>` marker on the reading line — the same established mechanism used by `_store/hlc.py`, `llm/gate_context.py`, and `_commands/session_id.py` — so the read is owned and self-documenting rather than whitelisted. Either way their `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` entries are removed (no path remains as a `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` row). `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` reports zero findings for these paths with those entries gone and no path-glob exception. The subsystem's behavioral suites stay green; redacted operation-snapshot fingerprints / provider-neutral outcomes are unchanged except recorded, justified deltas.\n\n## Plan\n1. For each below-seam read in the listed files, classify as cut-to-seam or register-owned; for cut-to-seam, thread the value from the composition seam rather than reading ambient `os.environ`/`os.getenv`/`load_config` below it.\n2. Remove the corresponding entries for these files from `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` in `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py`.\n3. Run `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` and the subsystem behavioral suites (tests/unit signing/opcert/logging suites); keep green.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- Held-out test `tests/scripts/test_residual_drain_seam_clean_heldout.py` asserts `check_config_ownership.check(check_config_ownership.REPO_ROOT)` returns no finding string containing any of the 9 listed paths, AND that none of the 9 listed paths remain as `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows (per-path membership check). It does NOT assert the whole list is EMPTY — the 2 residual rows are `binding_lifecycle.py` (owned by S7.3.a / `01d8-c18d-b229-419a`), outside this slice. RED now (entries present + reads below seam).\n- The subsystem behavioral suites (tests/unit signing/opcert/logging suites + the grounding suites) stay green after the cutover — they are the correctness oracle the AST gate supplements.\n- Redacted operation-snapshot fingerprints before/after are equal except recorded deltas.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nNo stored ticket/event/binding format changes. A legacy facade is removed only after its focused suite passes; until then rollback selects the facade.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] No direct ambient config/credential read, backend reload, or configurable default remains below the approved seam in the 9 listed files; each is either cut-to-seam or annotated in place with an inline `# read-via: <reason>` marker (kill-switch / test-only control), and no path remains as a `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` row.\n- [x] The `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` entries for these 9 files are removed from `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py` (the only residual rows are the 2 `binding_lifecycle.py` entries owned by S7.3.a / `01d8-c18d-b229-419a`), and `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` passes with no path-glob exception (proven by the held-out `test_residual_drain_seam_clean_heldout.py`).\n- [x] The subsystem behavioral suites (tests/unit signing/opcert/logging + grounding suites) pass after the cutover; redacted operation-snapshot fingerprints / provider-neutral outcomes are unchanged except recorded approved deltas.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_logging.py","reason":"residual-drain: route below-seam config/credential reads to the approved seam or register owned; drain LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS to empty"},{"path":"src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py","reason":"residual-drain: route below-seam config/credential reads to the approved seam or register owned; drain LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS to empty"},{"path":"src/rebar/_operation_config.py","reason":"residual-drain: route below-seam config/credential reads to the approved seam or register owned; drain LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS to empty"},{"path":"src/rebar/mirror_guard.py","reason":"residual-drain: route below-seam config/credential reads to the approved seam or register owned; drain LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS to empty"},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/app.py","reason":"residual-drain: route below-seam config/credential reads to the approved seam or register owned; drain LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS to empty"},{"path":"src/rebar/signing.py","reason":"residual-drain: route below-seam config/credential reads to the approved seam or register owned; drain LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS to empty"},{"path":"scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py","reason":"residual-drain: route below-seam config/credential reads to the approved seam or register owned; drain LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS to empty"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_residual_drain_seam_clean_heldout.py","reason":"residual-drain: route below-seam config/credential reads to the approved seam or register owned; drain LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS to empty"},{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/harness.py","reason":"residual-drain: route below-seam config/credential reads to the approved seam or register owned; drain LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS to empty"},{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/oracle.py","reason":"residual-drain: route below-seam config/credential reads to the approved seam or register owned; drain LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS to empty"},{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/resolve.py","reason":"residual-drain: route below-seam config/credential reads to the approved seam or register owned; drain LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS to empty"},{"path":"scripts/check_config_ownership.py","reason":"residual-drain: register grounding/resolve.py + grounding/oracle.py as composition-root seams in the gate"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_residual_drain_happy.py","reason":"residual-drain: happy-path structural spec for the drain"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","1b07-bf4d-4aca-41c4"],["depends_on","6633-219e-988a-42f6"],["depends_on","9515-ffa1-5272-4310"],["depends_on","9e42-78f7-c164-4bc8"],["depends_on","d074-ab22-e37a-4480"],["parent","075b-1479-dcb7-40ab"],["relates_to","80a7-7832-83d2-44e8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"075b-1479-dcb7-40ab","parent_status_uuid":"637eaa1d-c0b5-48da-bf5d-11cf2d2cd09d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ed65-a3d7-1aeb-4c36","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-04 S7.3.f — residual-drain cutover: route below-seam config reads through seams","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["14e9d565-8097-48e3-a6d0-2a8c231d6c42","e769896e-3e58-4acb-b899-f7ce692cdd40","fdf0930b-ee15-4a44-b1d9-070e62ca65d6","f4926938-ba5b-4c32-936e-a58f11d2e2ae","c7052577-dbc8-4395-b12f-d5c5f9616a37","dca8923e-8f76-49ba-8d28-3469c89827e3","8e683333-81e9-4001-9214-69